      "integration_contracts": [
        "Retain the reviewed eleven-module Physlib grant as inherited grounding; the scalar-composability repair directly imports no Physlib module, and the umbrella import Physlib remains forbidden.",
        "Reuse the released ChemistryLib.Units.Quantity, PositiveQuantity, Volume, Amount, AFPS2017.Flow.FlowRate, and their explicit value projections; do not create a parallel units or scalar-wrapper system.",
        "Derive the reported 5.6 mmol scalar value from the released factor-ten and computed-amount theorems, preserve the reported-versus-computed inequality, and do not silently correct the supplementary source.",
        "Treat flowVolume_hydraulicDuration_value as an ideal hydraulic calculation. Any statement about actual delivered volume must require an explicit ConstantFlowModel witness.",
        "Add only new repair-family modules and preserve all twenty-one authenticated prerequisite source files byte-for-byte.",
        "Use narrow imports and standard Mathlib reasoning only; do not infer experimental success, purity, identity, yield, pump performance, or transport behavior from scalar arithmetic."
      ],
